.\" Leon Build Tool \- Man Page
.TH LBT 1 "2026-08-08" "lbt 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lbt \- Leon Build Tool: discover boot entries, build ESP/ISO/IMG images, query geometry, control build/keys, and inspect the live machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lbt
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.br
.B lbt
.B info
.RI [ dump ]
.br
.B lbt
.B discover
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B lbt
.BR write " iso | img | esp"
.RB [ \-\-rootfs " dir ] [ \-\-out " file ] [ \-\-label " name ] [ \-\-size " " MiB ] [ \-\-arch " arch ]"
.br
.B lbt
.BR build " all | boot | kernel | lbt"
.RB [ \-\-arch " arch ]"
.br
.B lbt
.BR xfer " esp | stage"
.RB [ \-\-source " dir ] [ \-\-dest " dir ]"
.br
.B lbt
.BR keys " setup | sign | esl | verify"
.RB [ \-\-keydir " dir ] [ \-\-path " file ] [ \-\-out " file ] [ \-\-cert " pem ]"
.br
.B lbt
.I command
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RB [ flags ]
.br
See the
.B COMMANDS
section below for the full default command tree and the
.B FLAGS
section for the shared flag vocabulary.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lbt
is the host-side companion to the Leon bootloader and the 
.BR lbc (1)
boot-configuration tool. It introspects the live machine (block devices, EFI
System Partitions, boot entries, framebuffer and BGRT logo geometry), builds
bootable ESP/ISO/IMG images using pure-Rust FAT and GPT writers, builds the
bootloader, kernel, and itself, manages Secure Boot keys, and inspects the
host environment, filesystems, boot log, and firmware.
.PP
Boot configuration and boot control (the boot-manager menu, staging, the boot
config) moved to the sibling
.B lbc
binary \- see
.BR lbc (1).
Everything `lbt` needs for discovery, geometry, and imaging is discovered from
the live system at run time (\fIlsblk\fR and \fI/sys\fR); nothing is assumed or
invented.
.PP
The command line is parsed by a custom, table-driven dispatcher. Every command
supports short flags, long flags, aliases, and positional arguments freely at
any depth, and flags may appear before, between, or after subcommand tokens.
Every short flag character maps to exactly one long flag name, and every long
flag is consistently either a boolean or a value, so the same vocabulary is
valid across the whole tree.
.SH COMMANDS
The default build (without the optional
.B cps
feature) exposes the following namespaces. Each namespace also has a
single-letter alias command at the root (see the
.B ALIASES
section below).
.SS discover
.I lbt discover
auto-detects every EFI System Partition and its boot entries.
.TP
.B discover
List block devices (name, kind, filesystem, mount point), ESPs, and boot
entries. Detection is strict: `.efi` files must validate as PE/COFF
(`MZ` + `PE\e0\e0`) and ELF files must contain the `EFI stub` marker in the
first 64 KiB to be accepted as an EFI-stub kernel.
.TP
.B discover \-\-json
Emit the same information as machine-readable JSON with the keys
.BR devices ,
.BR esps ,
and
.BR boot_entries .
.PP
In addition to enumerating mounted ESPs, Leon scans common
.I /boot
locations
.RI ( /boot ,
.IR /boot/efi ,
.IR /boot/EFI )
recursively for EFI-capable files and includes them as candidate boot entries.
Entries are also read from systemd-boot
.RI ( EFI/systemd/loader/entries/*.conf
title lines) and GRUB
.RI ( grub.cfg
menuentry lines). The same physical file found under two spellings (e.g. an
ESP-relative path and an absolute
.I /boot/efi
path) is deduplicated so it appears only once, with the ESP-relative form
winning.
.SS info
.I lbt info
prints the current framebuffer and BGRT logo geometry.
.TP
.B info \fIdump\fR
With a path to a geometry record (\fIbootinfo.json\fR written by the
bootloader to
.IR \eEFI\eleon ),
print the captured geometry instead of the live one.
.TP
.B info
Without an argument, read live geometry from
.I /sys
.RI ( /sys/class/graphics/fb0
and
.IR /sys/firmware/acpi/bgrt ).
Fails loudly if no live framebuffer is available rather than guessing.
.PP
The geometry is also available through the
.B geometry
.
.BR show " / " geometry " " bgr
commands and the
.B json " " info
and
.B json " " all
commands.
.SS geometry
.TP
.B geometry show
Print the framebuffer + BGRT geometry (same as
.BR "info" ).
.TP
.B geometry bgr
Print only the BGRT logo geometry.
.SS write / image
Build bootable images from a rootfs directory. The ESP image is a
single-FAT-partition GPT disk written natively (no mtools); the IMG image is a
GPT disk with a FAT ESP partition plus an ext4 root partition populated
directly from the rootfs; the ISO image is an El Torito / hybrid ISO. The FAT
and GPT writers are pure Rust; only the ISO assembly
.RB ( xorriso
or
.RB genisoimage )
and the ext4 root partition
.RB ( mkfs.ext4 )
call host tools.
.TP
.B write iso \fR[\fB\-\-rootfs \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-out \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-\-label \fIname\fR]
Build a bootable ISO from a rootfs. The UEFI El Torito boot image is a small
FAT volume carrying the bootloader from
.I EFI/BOOT
(BOOTX64 or BOOTAA64). If neither loader is present, a data-only ISO is built
with a warning. When
.B xorriso
is available the ISO is made hybrid (bootable from USB too) using an
installed
.I isohdpfx.bin
MBR if present; otherwise
.B genisoimage
is used as a fallback. Defaults:
.I leon.iso
and label
.IR LEON .
.TP
.B write img \fR[\fB\-\-rootfs \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-out \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-\-size \fIMiB\fR]
Build a GPT disk image from a rootfs: a 64 MiB FAT ESP partition at 1 MiB plus
an ext4 root partition populated directly from the rootfs directory via
.BR "mkfs.ext4 -d"
(no mount, no privileges). Defaults:
.I leon.img
and size
.IR 1024 .
.TP
.B write esp \fR[\fB\-\-rootfs \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-out \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-\-size \fIMiB\fR] [\fB\-\-arch \fIarch\fR]
Build an ESP (EFI System Partition) disk image: a single-FAT-partition GPT
disk. When no
.B \-\-rootfs
is given, the repo's staged ESP tree
.I build/esp
(created by
.BR "lbc boot stage" )
is used. Defaults:
.I leon-esp.img
and size
.IR 64 .
These commands are also reachable as
.B lbt iso
(or
.BR x ),
.BR "lbt image iso/img/esp"
(or
.BR I ),
and
.BR "lbt w".
.SS build / xfer
.B lbt build
builds the bootloader, EFI-stub kernel, and the lbt host tool, mirroring the
Makefile targets in pure Rust.
.TP
.B build all \fR[\fB\-\-arch \fIarch\fR]
Build the bootloader, EFI-stub kernel, and lbt.
.TP
.B build boot \fR[\fB\-\-arch \fIarch\fR]
Build the UEFI bootloader
.RI ( lbl.efi )
for the given (or host) architecture.
.TP
.B build kernel \fR[\fB\-\-arch \fIarch\fR]
Build the EFI-stub kernel
.RI ( lbl-kernel.efi ).
.TP
.B build lbt
Build the lbt host tool (native target).
.PP
Supported architectures are
.B amd64
.RI ( x86_64-unknown-uefi )
and
.B arm64
.RI ( aarch64-unknown-uefi ).
.TP
.B xfer esp \fR[\fB\-\-source \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-dest \fIdir\fR]
Copy the staged ESP tree onto a mounted ESP volume (default source
.IR build/esp ,
default dest
.IR /mnt/esp ).
.TP
.B xfer stage \fR[\fB\-\-source \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-dest \fIdir\fR]
Copy a staged tree into a plain directory (default source
.IR build/esp ,
default dest
.IR esp ).
.SS keys / sign
.I lbt keys
manages Secure Boot keys and signatures, wrapping
.BR openssl " / " sbsign " / " sbverify " / " cert-to-efi-sig-list .
.TP
.B keys setup \fR[\fB\-\-keydir \fIdir\fR]
Generate a PK/KEK/db key set (RSA-2048 X.509, 10 years) under
.I keys
by default.
.TP
.B keys sign \fR[\fB\-\-keydir \fIdir\fR] \fB\-\-path \fIfile\fR [\fB\-\-out \fIfile\fR]
Sign an EFI image with the db key (default output
.IR file.signed ).
.TP
.B keys esl \fB\-\-cert \fIpem\fR
Emit an EFI Signature List
.RI ( cert.esl )
for a certificate.
.TP
.B keys verify \fB\-\-cert \fIpem\fR \fB\-\-path \fIfile\fR
Verify an EFI image signature against a certificate.
.SS env
.I lbt env
reports the host environment and prerequisites.
.TP
.B env show
Print the host environment: OS, PATH, SHELL, TERM, USER, host architecture, and
the availability of every key tool.
.TP
.B env check
Verify host prerequisites. The key tools are
.IR cargo ,
.IR rustup ,
.IR dd ,
.IR mkfs.ext4 ,
.IR mformat ,
.IR mcopy ,
.IR xorriso ,
.IR sgdisk ,
.IR openssl ,
.IR sbsign ,
.IR objcopy ,
and
.IR qemu-system-x86_64 .
.TP
.B env tool \fB\-\-name \fIname\fR
Locate a host tool on PATH and print its path.
.SS fs / rootfs
.I lbt fs
inspects directories and files; 
.I lbt rootfs
inspects root filesystems.
.TP
.B fs ls \fR[\fB\-\-path \fIdir\fR]
List a directory (default current directory).
.TP
.B fs info \fR[\fB\-\-path \fIpath\fR]
Stat a file or directory: kind, size, permissions, inode, modification time.
.TP
.B fs tree \fR[\fB\-\-path \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-depth \fIn\fR]
Print a directory tree (default depth 2).
.TP
.B rootfs show \fR[\fB\-\-path \fIdir\fR]
Describe a rootfs: total size, file count, and the presence of the
boot-critical paths
.IR EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI ,
.IR EFI/BOOT/BOOTAA64.EFI ,
.IR EFI/leon/kernel.efi ,
and
.IR EFI/leon/boot.toml .
.TP
.B rootfs check \fR[\fB\-\-path \fIdir\fR]
Validate a rootfs layout: require a bootloader (BOOTX64 or BOOTAA64) and the
EFI-stub kernel at
.IR EFI/leon/kernel.efi .
.TP
.B rootfs tree \fR[\fB\-\-path \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-depth \fIn\fR]
Inventory a rootfs (same as
.BR "fs tree" ).
.SS log
.I lbt log
shows, tails, clears, and searches the Leon boot log. The bootloader appends
to
.IR \evar\elogs\eleon\elog.md
on the boot volume, so by default these commands look at the repo's staged ESP
tree
.RI ( build/esp/var/logs/leon/log.md );
.B \-\-path
points at a mounted ESP's copy or anywhere else.
.TP
.B log show \fR[\fB\-\-path \fIfile\fR]
Print the whole boot log.
.TP
.B log tail \fR[\fB\-\-path \fIfile\fR]
Tail the boot log (polling), continuing as it grows and handling rotation.
.TP
.B log clear \fR[\fB\-\-path \fIfile\fR]
Truncate the boot log.
.TP
.B log find \fB\-\-pattern \fIpattern\fR [\fB\-\-path \fIfile\fR]
Search the boot log for lines containing the pattern, printing
.RI file:line: text .
.SS names
.I lbt names
lists and resolves discovered boot entries by label.
.TP
.B names list
List every discovered boot entry label.
.TP
.B names get \fB\-\-name \fIname\fR
Resolve one boot entry label to its on-ESP path.
.TP
.B names count
Count discovered boot entries.
.SS os
.I lbt os
reports host OS information.
.TP
.B os release
Print the OS release description (/etc/os-release).
.TP
.B os kernel
Print the running kernel version (
.BR uname -r ).
.TP
.B os id
Print the OS pretty name.
.SS json
.I lbt json
emits machine-readable JSON.
.TP
.B json info
Geometry as JSON (width, height, stride, format, logo), the same fields the
bootloader's
.I bootinfo.json
carries.
.TP
.B json discover \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Discovery result as JSON (esps + boot_entries).
.TP
.B json all
Everything (lbt version, framebuffer, logo, esps, boot_entries) as one JSON
document.
.SS query
.I lbt query
provides query front-ends.
.TP
.B query info
Query geometry (same as
.BR "info" ).
.TP
.B query esps
Query every ESP volume (same as
.BR "discover" 's
ESP section).
.SS usb
.I lbt usb
manages USB / block devices and flashing.
.TP
.B usb list
List USB / block devices.
.TP
.B usb flash \fB\-\-device \fI/dev/sdX\fR \fB\-\-path \fIimage.img\fR
Flash a disk image onto a block device (needs root). The image must be a whole
number of 512-byte sectors; the device must exist.
.TP
.B usb detect
Detect removable devices (from the sysfs
.I removable
attribute).
.SS firmware
.I lbt firmware
describes the firmware.
.TP
.B firmware info
Describe the firmware: UEFI vs BIOS/legacy, DMI vendor and product, and Secure
Boot state.
.TP
.B firmware secureboot
Report the Secure Boot state (from efivarfs).
.TP
.B firmware acpi
List the ACPI tables the firmware exposed.
.SS network
.TP
.B network check
Check network reachability with a plain TCP connect (no external tool) to
.IR 1.1.1.1:443
and
.IR 8.8.8.8:443 .
.SS devices
.TP
.B devices list
List block devices (same as
.BR "usb list" ).
.TP
.B devices esps
List ESP partitions (same as
.BR "query esps" ).
.SS esp
.TP
.B esp make \fR[\fB\-\-out \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-\-arch \fIarch\fR]
Build an ESP image (same as
.BR "write esp" ).
.TP
.B esp check \fR[\fB\-\-path \fIdir\fR]
Check an ESP volume (same as
.BR "fs info" ).
.TP
.B esp find
Find ESP volumes (same as
.BR "query esps" ).
.SS help
.TP
.B help all
Print the full command reference: every leaf command with its flags.
.TP
.B help tree
Print the command tree as an indented outline.
.TP
.B help command \fB\-\-name \fIname\fR
Describe one command (matched by canonical name or alias).
.SS alias
.TP
.B alias list
List every command alias declared in the tree.
.SS version
.TP
.B version
Print the version (
.BI lbt " " VERSION ).
Also reachable as
.BR "lbt -v" " / " "lbt --version" .
.SH FLAGS
The following flags are shared across the whole command tree. Each short
character maps to exactly one long name, and each long name is consistently
either a boolean or a value.
.TP
.B -j, --json
Boolean. Emit machine-readable JSON.
.TP
.B -p, --path \fIpath\fR
Value. File or directory path.
.TP
.B -o, --out \fIfile\fR
Value. Output file.
.TP
.B -r, --rootfs \fIdir\fR
Value. Root filesystem directory.
.TP
.B -n, --name \fIname\fR
Value. Entry name.
.TP
.B -d, --dest \fIdir\fR
Value. Destination directory.
.TP
.B -a, --arch \fIarch\fR
Value. Architecture:
.B amd64
or
.BR arm64 .
.TP
.B -c, --config \fIfile\fR
Value. Config file path.
.TP
.B -k, --keydir \fIdir\fR
Value. Secure Boot key directory.
.TP
.B -l, --label \fIname\fR
Value. Volume label.
.TP
.B -s, --size \fIMiB\fR
Value. Size in MiB.
.TP
.B -D, --depth \fIn\fR
Value. Traversal depth.
.TP
.B -f, --pattern \fIpattern\fR
Value. Search pattern.
.TP
.B -e, --device \fIpath\fR
Value. Block device path.
.TP
.B -g, --source \fIdir\fR
Value. Source path.
.TP
.B -x, --display \fIname\fR
Value. Display name.
.TP
.B -y, --desc \fItext\fR
Value. Description.
.TP
.B -F, --func \fIfunc\fR
Value. Plugin hook function.
.TP
.B -A, --aliases \fIlist\fR
Value. Comma-separated aliases.
.TP
.B -K, --key \fIkey\fR
Value. Config key.
.TP
.B -V, --value \fIvalue\fR
Value. Config value.
.TP
.B -C, --cert \fIpem\fR
Value. Certificate PEM path.
.PP
Additionally
.B -v
/
.BR --version
/
.B -V
prints the version (intercepted at the root), and
.B -h
/
.B --help
prints help for the node reached.
